{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n39 modules directly under `tests/unit/` have a `<name>_heldout.py` twin. Once both oracles have been reviewed the split only doubles module count, duplicates identical helper definitions, and makes every rename touch two files. Across these 39 pairs exactly one test-function name collides (`tests/unit/test_plan_material_pin_config_heldout.py::test_unreadable_optional_config_warns_structurally_and_returns_false`, semantically identical to base `:20-31`) and 8 pairs carry helper/fixture/class definitions with differing bodies; every other colliding definition is identical. The pair list with per-pair rename sets, filtered from enumeration (2) of the test-suite epic's first comment, is itemised in this ticket's first comment. This story starts only after the test-suite epic's last story (E10a-S5, defectible-befuddling-sheldrake) and every code epic of this release that edits `tests/` are closed, because those epics edit these twin modules; its blocking links record that. Cites re-measured on origin/main 7927904a0: the 39 pairs, the single colliding test name, the 8 differing-definition pairs, and the 24-LOC pin_config twin were each re-counted from `git ls-files tests/unit/` and an AST diff of every pair, not sampled.\n\n## Approach\nDirectory: `tests/unit/` root — 39 pairs; 12 definition renames spread over 8 pairs (the differing definitions take the `_heldout` suffix), plus one whole-file deletion for the single test-name collision. The 12 are `_RecordingScheme`, `clean_registry`, `_envelope` (test_attest_registry.py); `_plan_verdict`, `store` (test_audit_serve.py); `store` (test_identity_3183.py); `_events`, `store` (test_identity_4e9d.py); `_run` (test_identity_ac7_bff8.py); `_keypair` (test_identity_bde5.py); `_head` (test_identity_ts2_09f9.py); `_cfg` (test_rp04_s6_opcert_startup.py). For each pair: `cat` the held-out module into the base under a `# ── held-out oracles (merged from <name>_heldout.py) ──` divider; keep the base module docstring and append the held-out docstring's \"what it proves\" paragraph; dedupe identical definitions (`pytestmark` counts here — keep the base copy); rename differing definitions and repoint their callers; `git rm` the held-out file. Rename rule: suffix the HELD-OUT definition `_heldout` (e.g. `_load_heldout`) and repoint its callers; keep the base copy of identical definitions. Exception: `tests/unit/test_plan_material_pin_config_heldout.py` (24 LOC) is deleted whole — its single test duplicates base `:20-31`, so nothing is appended to `tests/unit/test_plan_material_pin_config.py`. No test body changes.\n\n## Scope\nIn scope: the 39 base modules directly under `tests/unit/` named in the first comment and their 39 `_heldout` twins. Out of scope: every pair under `tests/unit/{metrics,workflow,reconciler}` (S2), `tests/interfaces/` and `tests/integration/` (S3), `tests/scripts/` (S4), the 78 unpaired held-out renames (S5), every file under `src/`, and any test body change.\n\n## Testing\nPer pair: `pytest --collect-only -q <base> <heldout>` before and `pytest --collect-only -q <base>` after — counts equal (both recorded on this ticket); `pytest <base>` green. `make test` green.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Zero paired twins remain in this directory: for each of the 39 pairs `git ls-files tests/unit/<base>_heldout.py` prints nothing (the unpaired `_heldout` modules in this directory are untouched here and renamed in S5).\n- [ ] Per-pair node counts reconcile: each merged base collects exactly the sum of the two prior counts, from the before/after `pytest --collect-only -q` runs recorded on this ticket.\n- [ ] `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --check` **exits 0** — this story introduces no unadmitted mechanism. (`tests/unit/test_audit_serve.py::_clean_ui_env` is base-only and stays; the one `_clean` autouse key that buckets `stale` belongs to S2.) **AMENDED 2026-10-31 — the original `shows new=0` form is unmeetable.** `new=N` counts ADMITTED entries as well as unadmitted ones, so a clean tree at current main (`73e90b296e2`) already reports `active=648 new=28 increased=0 stale=0` and exits 0. No implementation of this story could drive that to `new=0`, so the criterion would fail at the end regardless of the work. Exit 0 is the gate's real pass signal, which is the property this AC means to assert. Root cause filed as bug `6f24-3d47-b251-4905`.\n- [ ] `make verify` green."}},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1793478400264413001,"uuid":"3ae1d050-4925-4642-8b26-e01ee225f740"}